  },
  "body": "There is a attribute called \"emHeightDescent\" in the TextMetrics. The description of it is:\n\nThe distance from the horizontal line indicated by the textBaseline attribute to the lowest bottom of the em squares in the line box. (Zero if the given baseline is the top of that em square.)\n\nThere is a mistake here. In particular, when the given baseline is the top of the em square, then its distance to the lowest bottom of the em square cannot be 0. It should be changed to \"Zero if the given baseline is the bottom of that em square\".\n\nPlease review. @junov @annevk @domenic \n",
